Calgary Junior / Staff Accountant — Consolidated Market Requirements
Research scope: Recent Calgary-area Junior Accountant, Junior Staff Accountant, and Staff Accountant postings. Senior and Intermediate Accountant roles and highly specialized accounting positions were excluded.

75–100% of Postings Included These
These are the strongest common requirements and should form the core of a generalized Calgary Junior/Staff Accountant job description.
Core Accounting Responsibilities
•	Perform day-to-day accounting activities and maintain accurate, complete, and up-to-date financial records.
•	Prepare and post journal entries.
•	Perform bank and general ledger/account reconciliations and investigate discrepancies.
•	Assist with or perform month-end close activities, including journal entries, reconciliations, account analysis, and supporting schedules.
•	Process or support accounts payable and/or accounts receivable activities, including invoices, payments, customer/vendor accounts, and related records.
•	Maintain organized accounting documentation, schedules, and supporting records.
•	Review financial information for accuracy and completeness and resolve discrepancies.
•	Apply fundamental accounting principles and accounting-cycle knowledge in daily work.
Recent examples consistently combine reconciliations, journal entries/GL work, AP/AR, month-end, and accurate financial records.
Core Qualifications
•	Post-secondary education in Accounting, Finance, Business, or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant accounting knowledge/experience.
•	Previous accounting, bookkeeping, accounting-clerk, or related experience, depending on the level of the position.
•	Strong attention to detail and accuracy.
•	Strong organizational and time-management skills.
•	Ability to work independently while also working effectively as part of a team.
•	Strong written and verbal communication skills.
•	Ability to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities.
•	Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and standard Microsoft Office applications.
Attention to detail, organization, communication, teamwork/independence, accounting education or experience, and Excel recur across the current sample.

50–75% of Postings Included These
These are common enough that they would be reasonable to include in a broad Calgary Junior/Staff Accountant posting, but they should not be treated as universal requirements.
Additional Accounting Duties
•	Assist with financial reporting and preparation of financial statements or internal financial reports.
•	Prepare and maintain working papers and supporting schedules.
•	Assist with audit requests and provide documentation to internal or external auditors.
•	Perform account analysis and investigate unusual balances, discrepancies, or variances.
•	Assist with expense reports and employee expense processing.
•	Assist with customer/vendor inquiries and resolve routine accounting issues.
•	Support process improvements and improvements to accounting procedures and controls.
•	Assist with other accounting projects and ad hoc accounting duties as required.
•	Maintain accounting records in accordance with company policies and applicable accounting requirements.
For example, Rockpoint emphasizes month-end, journal entries, reconciliations, supporting schedules, and variance analysis; Avenge adds audit support and process/control improvements; Robert Half's current junior-accountant postings similarly include reporting, documentation, discrepancies, and special projects.

25–50% of Postings Included These
These are legitimate recurring requirements, but they appeared in only a minority of the comparable postings. They should therefore be considered secondary/preferred requirements, not universal requirements.
Additional Technical & Financial Responsibilities
•	Assist with GST, sales tax, or other government remittances/filings.
•	Assist with payroll-related accounting or payroll data processing.
•	Assist with budgeting, forecasting, or variance analysis.
•	Support quarter-end and year-end accounting activities in addition to regular month-end close.
•	Assist with accruals, prepaid expenses, depreciation, or other specific balance-sheet accounts.
•	Work with multiple entities, business units, or locations.
•	Assist with cash management, bank activity, or payment processing beyond routine AP.
•	Participate in broader financial analysis in addition to transactional accounting.
•	Work with external accountants, auditors, or other professional advisors as required.
For example, SAF includes quarter-end documents, financial statements, depreciation schedules, tax compliance, and auditors; CRL includes payroll, GST, budgeting and forecasting; Avenge includes payroll support and GST/government requirements. These are recurring, but not sufficiently universal to belong in the 50–75% group.

10–25% of Postings Included These
These appeared often enough to be relevant to the Calgary market, but should absolutely not be presented as standard requirements for every Junior/Staff Accountant.
Specialized / Preferred Qualifications
•	Progress toward or enrollment in the CPA program / CPA PEP.
•	Previous experience specifically in public practice or a CPA firm.
•	Experience with CaseWare, CaseView, Taxprep, Profile, Jazzit, or other public-practice software.
•	Experience with QuickBooks, Xero, Sage, Dynamics 365, or another specific accounting platform.
•	Experience preparing tax returns or compilation engagements.
•	Experience in a specific industry such as oil & gas, energy, construction, or investment/financial services.
•	Advanced Excel capabilities beyond normal accounting use.
•	Previous experience with a particular ERP system.
For example, ELEVATE's Junior Staff Accountant posting is heavily public-practice/compilation oriented and specifically calls for CaseWare, Jazzit, Profile and tax software, while Kirk Wormley similarly emphasizes CPA-firm experience and public-practice software. Avenge, meanwhile, specifically mentions Dynamics 365 and CPA progression. Those are real Calgary-market requirements, but they are clearly not universal Junior/Staff Accountant requirements.
Excluded — Below 10%
I would not include isolated requirements that appeared in only one posting unless the particular employer actually needs them.
Examples include:
•	Specific industry experience that is unique to one employer.
•	A particular accounting software package used by only one employer.
•	Specialized capital/inventory accounting.
•	Specialized compilation/tax engagement requirements.
•	Very specific regulatory or reporting frameworks tied to one company.
•	Unusual language requirements.
•	Highly specific experience with a particular transaction type or business model.





These may be appropriate for an individual employer's posting, but including them in a "common Calgary Junior/Staff Accountant" profile would distort the market picture.
Consolidated Job Posting Based on the Research
Junior / Staff Accountant
We are seeking a detail-oriented and motivated Junior / Staff Accountant to support the day-to-day accounting operations of our organization. This role is well suited to an early-career accounting professional who wants to build strong practical experience across general accounting, reconciliations, accounts payable and receivable, month-end close, and financial reporting.
Responsibilities
•	Maintain accurate and complete accounting records.
•	Prepare and post routine journal entries.
•	Perform bank, general ledger, and other account reconciliations and investigate discrepancies.
•	Assist with month-end close activities, including reconciliations, account analysis, journal entries, accruals, and supporting schedules.
•	Process and support accounts payable and accounts receivable activities, including invoices, payments, customer/vendor accounts, and related documentation.
•	Maintain organized accounting files, working papers, schedules, and supporting documentation.
•	Review accounting information for accuracy and completeness.
•	Assist with financial reporting and preparation of internal financial information.
•	Assist with audit requests and provide supporting documentation as required.
•	Assist with account analysis, variance investigation, and resolution of discrepancies.
•	Support accounting process improvements and internal controls.
•	Assist with expense processing and other accounting activities as required.
•	Support year-end and other reporting requirements.
•	Perform other accounting projects and duties as assigned.
Qualifications
•	Post-secondary education in Accounting, Finance, Business, or a related field, or equivalent relevant experience.
•	Previous experience in accounting, bookkeeping, accounts payable/receivable, or a related accounting role.
•	Strong understanding of fundamental accounting principles and the accounting cycle.
•	Strong Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Office skills.
•	Excellent attention to detail and accuracy.
•	Strong organizational and time-management skills.
•	Strong written and verbal communication skills.
•	Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team.
•	Ability to manage competing priorities and consistently meet deadlines.
•	Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.
•	Professional, dependable, and willing to learn and take on increasing responsibility.
Preferred / Additional Qualifications
•	Experience with an ERP or accounting software system.
•	Experience with GST or other tax-related accounting activities.
•	Experience supporting payroll or employee expenses.
•	Experience with budgeting, forecasting, or financial analysis.
•	Experience supporting audits and year-end procedures.
•	CPA program/CPA PEP progress or an interest in pursuing the CPA designation.
•	Public-practice or industry-specific accounting experience.
•	Experience with QuickBooks, Sage, Xero, CaseWare, Dynamics 365, or other accounting platforms.
The biggest correction from my previous version
The important change is that I would no longer characterize things like CPA progression, tax returns, public-practice software, fixed assets, intercompany accounting, or specialized industry experience as 25–75% requirements.
The research supports putting the true common denominator much more narrowly around:
Accounting fundamentals → AP/AR → journal entries → reconciliations → month-end → accurate records/documentation → Excel → attention to detail → organization → communication/teamwork.
That is the profile that appears to travel across the greatest number of Calgary Junior/Staff Accountant postings.

